# Design: Pi agent source (T037)

## Problem
Add the third ingestion source from the corrected, verified layout:
sessions are global under ~/.pi/agent/sessions/<encoded-cwd>/, one
append-only JSONL per session; the third-party "project-local .pi/"
claim is wrong. Identity and usage rules had to follow the captured
0.84.2/1.5.2 samples, not writeups.

## Approach
- Reuse the Codex header-first rule: the `session` entry at offset 0
  names the session; no later entry repeats it. Parses past offset 0
  take the id from the committed first record (store.SourceState).
- MessageID is the assistant `responseId`, which makes the store's
  one-row-per-(session, message_id) usage table sum per-response
  exactly, with no Claude-Code-style dedupe. An error response has no
  responseId, so its all-zero usage writes no row.
- Usage validity check: input + cacheRead + output == totalTokens
  (identity held in every verified record, cacheRead non-zero in
  one). Pi's `input` therefore excludes cache reads, unlike Codex.
  reasoning and cacheWrite stay unmapped until their subset
  relations are verified (NOTES.md open questions).
- The 1.5.2 `system` entry (harness preamble, sections, toolsAdded)
  contributes no search text: it is identical across sessions and
  would pollute BM25; its shape lands in metadata.

## Key Trade-offs
- Strict usage-sum validation drops a whole usage when a provider
  counts reasoning or cacheWrite outside the verified identity —
  doctrine: ambiguous counts count nothing.
- The lossy encoded-cwd directory is never decoded; the header cwd
  is authoritative, so colliding directories stay distinct sessions.
- --session-dir runs are not discoverable from the environment; the
  persistent env vars cover the default, -pi-root covers the rest.

